 (42,124,'Quadratic injectivity reminder diagrams','The general unrestricted quadratic fails the horizontal-line test; the restricted example2(x−3)^2−5 on x>=3 is injective with vertex(3,−5). Restricting to a monotone side is sufficient, but an injective interval need not BEGIN at the turning point. Completing the square is useful, not a logical requirement for every inverse method.',[ONEONE,INVERSE],'graph',[('expand(2*(x-3)**2-5)','2*x**2-12*x+13')],None,'teaching-figure'),
